## Why This Is Asked
Tests ability to design end-to-end CAPA for privacy-policy drift in a multi-tenant, partner‑integrated data plane. Requires data modeling, lifecycle management, API surfaces, observability, and rollout safety.

## Key Concepts
- CAPA data model including lineage and policy versions
- Region/tenant-aware metrics
- Lifecycle state machine and RCA templates
- Canary rollout and rollback safeguards

## Code Example
```javascript
type CAPA = {
  id: string;
  tenantId: string;
  region: string;
  policyVersion: string;
  evidenceRefs: string[];
  dataLineage: string;
  rootCause?: string;
  correctiveAction?: string;
  containmentStatus: 'detected'|'investigating'|'contained'|'verified'|'closed';
  timestamps: { detected: string; updated?: string; closed?: string };
}
```

## Follow-up Questions
- How would you test the canary rollout for a policy upgrade in this scenario?
- What data access controls and retention would you enforce during CAPA investigations?

## Why This Is Asked
Tests ability to design end-to-end CAPA for a hardware-leaning, safety-critical system with OTA risk, cross-region data, and telemetry traces. Emphasizes traceability, regionalization, and safe validation.

## Key Concepts
- Immutable evidence ledger (incidentId, firmwareVersion, OTA bundle, sensor flags, region, vehicle_type)
- Region-aware CAPA lifecycle state machine
- Minimal REST API to link CAPAs with logs/traces
- Region- and vehicle-type metrics: recurrence rate, MTTR, false-positive rate
- RCA template and canary rollout with rollback

## Code Example
```javascript
// Minimal Express route to create a CAPA
const express = require('express');
const app = express();
app.use(express.json());
app.post('/capa', (req, res) => {
  const { incidentId, firmwareVersion, otaBundle, region, vehicleType, evidenceLinks } = req.body;
  // Persist CAPA object with linked evidence in DB (pseudo)
  const capaId = generateId();
  saveCapa({ capaId, incidentId, firmwareVersion, otaBundle, region, vehicleType, evidenceLinks, status: 'DETECTED' });
  res.status(201).json({ id: capaId });
});
```

## Follow-up Questions
- How would you model cross-region deduplication of CAPAs when two regions report the same incident?
- What metrics and experiments would verify the efficacy of the canary rollout before global deployment?

## Why This Is Asked
This question tests end-to-end CAPA design for data-label drift impacting model training with region-specific effects, governance signals, and remediation validation.

## Key Concepts
- CAPA data model with evidence, lineage, owners
- Region-aware lifecycle: detect → contain → remediate → verify; per-region SLAs
- REST API for CAPA creation/update with logs/traces and policy links
- Region metrics: containment MTTR, drift recurrence, false-positive drift alerts
- RCA template and canary rollout plan for labeling changes

## Code Example
```javascript
type CAPA = {
  id: string;
  region: string;
  evidence: string[];
  lineage: string;
  owners: string[];
  status: "detect" | "contain" | "remediate" | "verify";
  slaHours: number;
  policyLinks?: string[];
}
